## MCP Server: Jina AI (`user-Jina_AI`)

**Best for:** Multi-perspective web search, page reading, academic papers, image search, content reranking

| Tool | Purpose | Key Params | Best For |
|------|---------|------------|----------|
| `search_web` | Web search | `query` (string or array), `num` (1-100), `tbs` (time), `location`, `gl`, `hl` | General web search with geo/language targeting |
| `parallel_search_web` | Run up to 5 searches simultaneously | `searches` (array of search configs) | Exploring multiple angles of a topic at once |
| `read_url` | Extract page content as markdown | `url` (single or array), `withAllLinks`, `withAllImages` | Reading articles, bypassing paywalls |
| `parallel_read_url` | Read up to 5 URLs simultaneously | `urls` (array) | Comparing content across multiple sources |
| `expand_query` | Expand a query into multiple variants | `query` | Getting diverse search angles before parallel search |
| `sort_by_relevance` | Rerank documents by relevance | `query`, `documents` (array), `top_n` | Filtering search results to most relevant |
| `search_images` | Image search | `query`, `return_url` | Finding logos, diagrams, visual references |
| `search_arxiv` | Academic paper search | `query` (string or array), `num` | Finding research papers, scientific references |
| `capture_screenshot_url` | Screenshot a webpage | `url`, `firstScreenOnly` | Visual inspection of websites |
| `extract_pdf` | Extract figures/tables from PDFs | `id` or `url`, `type` (figure/table/equation) | Extracting visuals from academic papers |
| `primer` | Get session context (time, location) | (none) | Getting localized context for time/geo-aware responses |

**Jina vs Tavily:** Jina excels at parallel operations (up to 5 concurrent searches/reads), academic paper search, image search, and content reranking. Tavily excels at deep research synthesis and site crawling.

